    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0567" n="535" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v13p1/pg535"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower Library, Dulles papers, “Telephone
                    Conversations”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversation Between the
                        Secretary of State and the French Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bonnet</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d259-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1953-05-02">May 2,
                        1953</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Secretary telephoned Amb. Bonnet (who was at Warrenton, Va.) and told him
                    that he was planning to issue a statement this afternoon about Laos.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d259-f2"/> The Secretary read the proposed statement to Amb.
                    Bonnet, who commented that it was very good and he thought it would bring a
                    little encouragement to Laos.</p>
                <p>The Secretary told him that he hoped his Government would reconsider their
                    position on the U.N. He said that he had had a meeting with several
                    Congressional leaders this morning and they had asked why Laos did not report
                    the matter to the U.N. and the only answer he could give them was that the
                    French were afraid it would provoke a debate on colonialism. He said that the
                    Congressmen were suspicious that there was something wrong there if the French
                    were that afraid.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador said that they feel all that they would get from the U.N. anyway
                    is moral help. He said that they were still studying the question, however, and
                    that there would probably be a statement in a few days.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
